#
# bpsec-all-multinode-test.bsl
#
# BSL (Bundle Security Library) multinode BPSec integration test.
# Verifies BIB (integrity) and BCB (confidentiality) security processing
# across a 3-node topology using LTP convergence layer.
#
# Topology:
#   Node 2 (ipn:2.*) --LTP--> Node 3 (ipn:3.*) --LTP--> Node 4 (ipn:4.*)
#
# Security design (RFC 9172 compliant):
#   Per RFC 9172 Section 4.7, a single security source MUST NOT apply
#   separate BIB and BCB to the same target block. Instead:
#     - BIB targets the PRIMARY block (tgt 0) for integrity
#     - BCB targets the PAYLOAD block (tgt 1) for confidentiality
#   This ensures each security service operates on a different block.
#
# BSL policy is loaded at startup via "m bsl" in each node's bprc.
#   Node 2 (source):
#     - BIB source on primary (tgt 0) for 2->3 and 2->4
#     - BCB source on payload (tgt 1) for 2->3 and 2->4
#   Node 3 (waypoint/dest for 2->3, relay for 2->4):
#     - BCB verifier at CLIN (validates ASB, does NOT decrypt)
#     - BIB acceptor at APPOUT for primary (verifies HMAC)
#     - BCB acceptor at APPOUT for payload (decrypts)
#     - BCB relay verifier at CLIN for 2->4 transit traffic
#   Node 4 (dest for 2->4):
#     - BCB verifier at CLIN (validates ASB, does NOT decrypt)
#     - BIB acceptor at APPOUT for primary (verifies HMAC)
#     - BCB acceptor at APPOUT for payload (decrypts)
#
# Note: BIB verifiers are NOT used at CLIN because BIB on the primary
# block does not depend on BCB processing order (BIB targets a different
# block than BCB). However, BIB verification at CLIN is unnecessary for
# this test since the acceptor at APPOUT performs the same check. BCB
# verifiers at CLIN perform a lightweight ASB validation without decrypting.
#
# Tests:
#   Test 1 - Small bundle node 2->3 with BIB(primary)+BCB(payload)
#   Test 2 - Small bundle node 2->3, verify BSL initialization
#   Test 3 - SKIPPED (wrong-key test not feasible with NULL_SUITES)
#   Test 4 - Small bundle node 2->3 (baseline without dynamic rule changes)
#   Test 5 - Large ~4MB file node 2->3 with BIB(primary)+BCB(payload)
#   Test 6 - Small bundle node 2->4 via node 3 relay, BCB relay verification
#   Test 7 - Anonymous bundle node 2->4 via node 3 relay
#   Test 8 - Small bundle node 2->4 via node 3 relay (exercises SDR BTSD
#            read path for BIB on primary at acceptor)
#
# Originally based on test by Scott Burleigh, April 12, 2010.
# Adapted to BSP by Ryan Brown, August 2011.
# Adapted to BSL multinode test with per-node policy files.

